{"v":2,"s":"c","w":3,"steps":[{"t":"read","h":"Shells and how many electrons fit","b":"<p>Electrons sit in <b>shells</b> (ljuske, energetski nivoi) numbered n = 1, 2, 3, 4… (also called K, L, M, N). A shell holds at most <b>2n²</b> electrons: 2, 8, 18, 32.</p><p>Shells are split into <b>subshells</b> (podnivoi): s holds 2, p holds 6, d holds 10 electrons.</p><div class=\"callout\">A hotel: lower floors (shells) fill first, and each room (orbital) takes at most two guests.</div>"},{"t":"read","h":"Filling order","b":"<p>Electrons fill subshells from the lowest energy up:</p><div class=\"fx\">1s → 2s → 2p → 3s → 3p → 4s → 3d → 4p</div><p>Note that <b>4s fills before 3d</b>. Examples:</p><ul><li>C (6): 1s² 2s² 2p²</li><li>Na (11): 1s² 2s² 2p⁶ 3s¹ — by shells 2, 8, 1</li><li>Ca (20): 1s² 2s² 2p⁶ 3s² 3p⁶ 4s²</li></ul>"},{"t":"read","h":"Valence electrons","b":"<p><b>Valence electrons</b> (valentni elektroni) are in the outermost shell. They decide how an element reacts.</p><p>Noble gases have a full outer shell (8, or 2 for He) and almost never react. Other atoms react to reach the same stable configuration — the <b>octet rule</b>: metals lose electrons, nonmetals gain or share them.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 320 216\" text-anchor=\"middle\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Chlorine-35: shells 2, 8, 7. The seven outer (valence) electrons decide how it reacts — it wants one more.\"><defs><marker id=\"ah\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" class=\"ink\"/></marker><marker id=\"ahc\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" class=\"a\"/></marker></defs><circle cx=\"160\" cy=\"104\" r=\"34\" class=\"km\"/><circle cx=\"160.0\" cy=\"70.0\" r=\"4.5\" class=\"a\"/><circle cx=\"160.0\" cy=\"138.0\" r=\"4.5\" class=\"a\"/><circle cx=\"160\" cy=\"104\" r=\"60\" class=\"km\"/><circle cx=\"160.0\" cy=\"44.0\" r=\"4.5\" class=\"a\"/><circle cx=\"202.4\" cy=\"61.6\" r=\"4.5\" class=\"a\"/><circle cx=\"220.0\" cy=\"104.0\" r=\"4.5\" class=\"a\"/><circle cx=\"202.4\" cy=\"146.4\" r=\"4.5\" class=\"a\"/><circle cx=\"160.0\" cy=\"164.0\" r=\"4.5\" class=\"a\"/><circle cx=\"117.6\" cy=\"146.4\" r=\"4.5\" class=\"a\"/><circle cx=\"100.0\" cy=\"104.0\" r=\"4.5\" class=\"a\"/><circle cx=\"117.6\" cy=\"61.6\" r=\"4.5\" class=\"a\"/><circle cx=\"160\" cy=\"104\" r=\"86\" class=\"km\"/><circle cx=\"160.0\" cy=\"18.0\" r=\"4.5\" class=\"a\"/><circle cx=\"227.2\" cy=\"50.4\" r=\"4.5\" class=\"a\"/><circle cx=\"243.8\" cy=\"123.1\" r=\"4.5\" class=\"a\"/><circle cx=\"197.3\" cy=\"181.5\" r=\"4.5\" class=\"a\"/><circle cx=\"122.7\" cy=\"181.5\" r=\"4.5\" class=\"a\"/><circle cx=\"76.2\" cy=\"123.1\" r=\"4.5\" class=\"a\"/><circle cx=\"92.8\" cy=\"50.4\" r=\"4.5\" class=\"a\"/><circle cx=\"160.0\" cy=\"104.0\" r=\"4\" class=\"mu\"/><circle cx=\"157.6\" cy=\"106.2\" r=\"4\" class=\"ge\"/><circle cx=\"160.4\" cy=\"99.4\" r=\"4\" class=\"mu\"/><circle cx=\"163.5\" cy=\"108.5\" r=\"4\" class=\"ge\"/><circle cx=\"153.5\" cy=\"102.8\" r=\"4\" class=\"mu\"/><circle cx=\"166.2\" cy=\"100.0\" r=\"4\" class=\"ge\"/><circle cx=\"157.9\" cy=\"111.8\" r=\"4\" class=\"mu\"/><circle cx=\"156.0\" cy=\"96.3\" r=\"4\" class=\"ge\"/><circle cx=\"168.8\" cy=\"107.2\" r=\"4\" class=\"mu\"/><circle cx=\"150.8\" cy=\"107.8\" r=\"4\" class=\"ge\"/><circle cx=\"164.4\" cy=\"94.5\" r=\"4\" class=\"mu\"/><circle cx=\"163.3\" cy=\"114.4\" r=\"4\" class=\"ge\"/><circle cx=\"150.1\" cy=\"98.3\" r=\"4\" class=\"mu\"/><circle cx=\"171.6\" cy=\"101.5\" r=\"4\" class=\"ge\"/><circle cx=\"152.9\" cy=\"114.1\" r=\"4\" class=\"mu\"/><circle cx=\"158.4\" cy=\"91.3\" r=\"4\" class=\"ge\"/><circle cx=\"170.1\" cy=\"112.5\" r=\"4\" class=\"mu\"/><circle cx=\"146.4\" cy=\"104.6\" r=\"4\" class=\"ge\"/><circle cx=\"169.9\" cy=\"94.1\" r=\"4\" class=\"mu\"/><circle cx=\"159.3\" cy=\"118.4\" r=\"4\" class=\"ge\"/><circle cx=\"150.6\" cy=\"92.7\" r=\"4\" class=\"mu\"/><circle cx=\"175.0\" cy=\"106.0\" r=\"4\" class=\"ge\"/><circle cx=\"147.3\" cy=\"112.8\" r=\"4\" class=\"mu\"/><circle cx=\"163.5\" cy=\"88.6\" r=\"4\" class=\"ge\"/><circle cx=\"168.0\" cy=\"118.0\" r=\"4\" class=\"mu\"/><circle cx=\"144.3\" cy=\"99.0\" r=\"4\" class=\"ge\"/><circle cx=\"175.3\" cy=\"97.0\" r=\"4\" class=\"mu\"/><circle cx=\"153.4\" cy=\"119.8\" r=\"4\" class=\"ge\"/><circle cx=\"154.1\" cy=\"87.6\" r=\"4\" class=\"mu\"/><circle cx=\"175.7\" cy=\"112.3\" r=\"4\" class=\"ge\"/><circle cx=\"142.5\" cy=\"108.6\" r=\"4\" class=\"mu\"/><circle cx=\"170.0\" cy=\"88.6\" r=\"4\" class=\"ge\"/><circle cx=\"163.1\" cy=\"122.4\" r=\"4\" class=\"mu\"/><circle cx=\"145.0\" cy=\"92.4\" r=\"4\" class=\"ge\"/><circle cx=\"179.2\" cy=\"102.4\" r=\"4\" class=\"mu\"/><circle cx=\"20\" cy=\"206\" r=\"4\" class=\"ge\"/><text x=\"28\" y=\"210\" text-anchor=\"start\">proton</text><circle cx=\"98\" cy=\"206\" r=\"4\" class=\"mu\"/><text x=\"106\" y=\"210\" text-anchor=\"start\">neutron</text><circle cx=\"182\" cy=\"206\" r=\"4.5\" class=\"a\"/><text x=\"190\" y=\"210\" text-anchor=\"start\">electron</text></svg><figcaption>Chlorine-35: shells 2, 8, 7. The seven outer (valence) electrons decide how it reacts — it wants one more.</figcaption></figure>"},{"t":"ex","q":"Write the configuration of chlorine (Z = 17) and predict its ion.","s":["Fill in order: 1s² 2s² 2p⁶ 3s² 3p⁵ (2+2+6+2+5 = 17).","By shells: 2, 8, 7 — so 7 valence electrons.","It needs 1 more for an octet, so it gains one electron."],"a":"1s² 2s² 2p⁶ 3s² 3p⁵, forms Cl⁻"},{"t":"mc","q":"Electron configuration of oxygen (Z = 8):","o":["1s² 2s² 2p⁴","1s² 2s⁶","1s² 2s² 2p⁶","1s² 2p⁶"],"a":0,"e":"2 + 2 + 4 = 8 electrons."},{"t":"num","q":"How many valence electrons does aluminium (Z = 13) have?","a":3,"u":"","e":"1s² 2s² 2p⁶ 3s² 3p¹ → 2 + 1 = 3 in the third shell."},{"t":"mc","q":"Which element has the shell distribution 2, 8, 2?","o":["Ne","Na","Mg","Si"],"a":2,"e":"2 + 8 + 2 = 12 electrons → Z = 12, magnesium."},{"t":"num","q":"Maximum number of electrons in the second shell (n = 2)?","a":8,"u":"","e":"2n² = 2·4 = 8."},{"t":"tf","q":"The 4s subshell fills before 3d.","a":true,"e":"4s has slightly lower energy, so potassium and calcium put electrons in 4s first."}]}